 "desc_header": "IN THIS LESSON",
 "lyrics": "A polar bear's skin is black (Polar Bears International); its hair is made of clear, hollow tubes, and its fat can be 2 to 4 inches thick (San Diego Zoo, 'Polar bear').\nPolar bears paddle with their broad front feet and can swim more than 60 miles without rest (San Diego Zoo, 'Polar bear'); their back legs steer like rudders; the paws are as big as dinner plates (Polar Bears International).\nHorses can doze standing up because a 'stay apparatus' locks their legs; they lie down for deep (REM) sleep (PetMD; Merck Veterinary Manual).\nA healthy foal stands within one hour of birth and nurses within two (Cornell University College of Veterinary Medicine).\nA giraffe has seven neck vertebrae, the same number as a human and almost every other mammal; each can be about 10 inches (25 cm) long (Bristol Zoo; San Diego Zoo).\nA giraffe's tongue can be up to 21 inches long (National Geographic Kids, 'Giraffe').",
 "script": "Hello, friends! I am Milo the bluebird.\nToday we are playing Yes or No!\nI will ask a question about an animal friend.\nIf you think yes, give a thumbs up. If you think no, shake your head.\nLet's practice. Yes or no. Am I a bluebird?\nYes! I am Milo the bluebird! Good job.\nAre you ready? Let's play!\nHere is the polar bear. Look at that white, fluffy fur.\nYes or no. Is a polar bear's skin white?\nNo! Here is the fun fact. Under the fur, a polar bear's skin is black!\nLook closer. Black skin, hiding under all that fur.\nAnd the fur is not really white. Each hair is clear, like glass!\nUnder the skin, there is a thick layer of fat. It keeps the polar bear warm in the icy cold.\nNext question. Yes or no. Can a polar bear swim?\nYes! Polar bears are super swimmers!\nLook at those big front paws. They work like paddles in the water.\nEach paw is as big as a dinner plate!\nA polar bear can swim a very, very long way, without stopping to rest!\nIts back legs steer, like the rudder of a boat.\nBrrr! The water is icy cold. But the polar bear stays warm.\nSay it with me. Polar bear skin is black!\nCan you paddle your paws like a polar bear? Paddle, paddle, paddle!\nQuick check! What color is a polar bear's skin? White? Or black?\nBlack! Black skin, under clear fur. Brilliant!\nClap your paws!\nHere is the horse. Clip, clop!\nYes or no. Can a horse sleep standing up?\nYes! Here is the fun fact. A horse can sleep standing up!\nBut how can it sleep without falling over?\nIts legs lock in place, so it does not fall over.\nYou have two legs. A horse has four! One, two, three, four.\nFor a big, deep sleep, the horse lies down on the soft ground.\nA horse does not sleep all night like you. It takes lots of tiny naps!\nNow look, a baby horse! A baby horse is called a foal.\nA foal can stand up on its wobbly legs when it is only one hour old!\nThe mama horse feeds her foal with her milk.\nNow you. Do you sleep standing up? Yes, or no?\nNo! You sleep lying down, in your cozy bed. But a horse can do both!\nSay it with me. Horses can sleep standing up!\nCan you stand very still and close your eyes? Shh. One, two, three.\nQuick check! For a big, deep sleep, does a horse stand up? Or lie down?\nIt lies down! Good remembering!\nNow wiggle and wake up. Good morning!\nHere is the giraffe. Look at that long, long neck!\nYes or no. Does a giraffe have the same number of neck bones as you?\nYes! Here is the fun fact. A giraffe has seven neck bones. And so do you!\nThe giraffe's neck bones are just much, much bigger. Each one is almost as long as a ruler!\nLet's count them. One, two, three, four, five, six, seven!\nNext question. Yes or no. Does a tiny mouse have seven neck bones too?\nYes! A mouse has seven. You have seven. And the giraffe has seven!\nAlmost every furry animal has seven neck bones. Big or small!\nLet's count on your fingers. One, two, three, four, five, six, seven!\nAnd the giraffe's tongue is long too. Even longer than a ruler!\nIt uses that long tongue to grab leaves from the tall, tall trees.\nSay it with me. Seven neck bones, just like me!\nCan you touch your neck? Gently now. Nod your head. Yes, yes, yes!\nQuick check! How many neck bones does a giraffe have? Five? Or seven?\nSeven! Just like you!\nHold up seven fingers. Hooray!\nWow! What a great game. Let's play one more time, super fast!\nGet ready!\nIs a polar bear's skin white?\nNo! It is black!\nCan a horse sleep standing up?\nYes! It can!\nDoes a giraffe have seven neck bones, like you?\nYes! Seven, just like you!\nYou learned so many new things today.\nPaddle like a polar bear. Stand still like a horse. And nod like a giraffe!\nWhich answer surprised you the most?\nOne last question. Yes or no. Did you have fun today?\nYes! Me too!\nThank you for playing with me. Bye-bye, friends! See you next time!",
